{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"body":"Evidence from lane-vcdedup's MCP writes on 2026-10-18 (all times PDT). Facts only; no cause established.\n\n- Writes that REACHED origin/tickets (server env eea68b7f): next-embattled-geese (3b27-8f4b) COMMENT 19:42:44, STATUS in_progress->closed 19:46:29, SIGNATURE 19:46:49. So the server was still publishing to the shared branch at 19:46:49, which bears on the \"about 19:40\" observation time in the description.\n- 19:58:44: MCP `create_ticket` returned id 2124-5954-4e80-4f72 with push_status `{\"state\":\"pending\",\"reason\":\"lock-timeout\",\"detail\":\"write lock stayed busy during push recovery\",\"remote_ref\":\"origin/tickets\",\"unpushed\":\"4\"}`. That ticket is ABSENT from origin/tickets on a fresh local fetch; it is stranded in the server clone. Recreated locally as daredevil-marginal-dodo (0521-7e68).\n- About 3 minutes later: the next MCP `create_ticket` failed with `flock: could not acquire lock after 181s (holder: host=boot-166d945d-7290-49bd-97fc-8fa0ed945692 pid=678 start=343361372 held=93s pid_state=live op=compact-sweep)`. Nothing was created (confirmed by local search). Recreated locally as talented-portable-sow (c912-f274).\n- Earlier async gate failures, same server: review_plan_start job started 14:37:46 ended `daemon-stopped` (\"async gate daemon stopped before recording a terminal result\"); a job started 15:13:28 ended `gate_congested`. Both re-ran cleanly afterwards.\n\nNot checked: whether pid 678's compact-sweep was running at 19:58:44, and whether the 4 unpushed commits include server-side compaction."},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1792379412730350001,"uuid":"96b93872-5a6c-4742-9043-f6f569615101"}